{"id": "EUVD-2026-101731", "enisaUuid": "d7325675-df85-3e0b-b7ac-da2564ed5005", "description": "n8n before 1.123.83, 2.x before 2.41.4, and 2.42.x before 2.42.1 contains a prototype pollution vulnerability in the AI workflow builder, which merges workflow connections using node names as object members without checking for reserved keys. Authenticated users can create nodes named __proto__ through the API and invoke the connect-nodes operation to pollute the global object prototype, disrupting the instance until restart.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T22:52:23", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T17:14:56", "baseScore": 6.0, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/security/advisories/GHSA-3p2g-2wpm-8h3g", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/n8n-before-1.123.83-2.41.4-and-2.42.1-prototype-pollution-via-ai-workflow-builder-connection-merge"], "aliases": ["GHSA-v3wp-jvw4-xcp3", "CVE-2026-110848"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.31, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "d38ce90e-1758-3366-a25e-13ab4c3f77e4", "product": {"name": "n8n", "vendor": {"name": "n8n-io"}}, "product_version": "2.42.0 <2.42.1"}, {"id": "fb787162-12fe-3f96-ad72-310bc1ed8683", "product": {"name": "n8n", "vendor": {"name": "n8n-io"}}, "product_version": "0 <1.123.83"}, {"id": "ff46b5ec-1f44-33c9-aec8-e070de9c17ad", "product": {"name": "n8n", "vendor": {"name": "n8n-io"}}, "product_version": "2.0.0 <2.41.4"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "9cb0bf08-4484-3454-b891-29f5e6b74d18", "vendor": {"name": "n8n-io"}}], "isExploited": false}